  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0225' contains four tables: Company, User, Request_Log, and User_Feedback.\nThe Company table is used to store information about companies. It includes columns for Authorization_Token (a string), Company_ID (an integer), Company_Name (a string), Creation_Time (a datetime), Modification_Time (a datetime), and Token_Hash_Value (an integer). The Company_ID is the primary key.\nThe User table is used to store information about users. It includes columns for Company_ID (an integer), Creation_Time (a datetime), Modification_Time (a datetime), Password_Hash_Value (an integer), Password_Salt_Value (a string), Permission_Level (a string), User_ID (an integer), and User_Name (a string). The User_ID is the primary key and Company_ID is a foreign key referencing the Company table.\nThe Request_Log table is used to store information about requests. It includes columns for Compression_Result (a blob), Probe_Information (a string), Request_Data (a string), Request_ID (an integer), Status (a string), Timestamp (a datetime), and User_ID (an integer). The Request_ID is the primary key and User_ID is a foreign key referencing the User table.\nFinally, the User_Feedback table is used to store feedback from users. It includes columns for Comment (a string), Creation_Time (a datetime), Feedback_ID (an integer), Rating (a float), and User_ID (an integer). The Feedback_ID is the primary key and User_ID is a foreign key referencing the User table. All columns allow null values and have default values where appropriate. The primary keys enforce entity integrity, foreign keys enforce referential integrity, and other constraints and indexes are used to maintain data integrity.",
  "gold_question": "Design and implement a database management system for an enterprise-level natural language processing (NLP) platform, which shall support:\n\nCompany management (store basic company information, authorization tokens and their hash values, record creation and modification timestamps),      \n\nUser management (store detailed user information, password salt values and their hash values, manage permissions and record creation and modification timestamps),\n\nRequest processing log recording (store request ID, user ID, status, timestamp, request data, compression results and probe information),\n\nand User feedback management (store rating, comments and creation timestamp).",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0225.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0225\nCREATE TABLE `company` (\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `authorization_token` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `company_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `modification_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `token_hash_value` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`company_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `company_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `modification_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password_hash_value` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password_salt_value` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `permission_level` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`company_id`) REFERENCES `company` (`company_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `request_log` (\n  `request_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `compression_result` blob DEFAULT NULL,\n  `probe_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `request_data` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `timestamp` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`request_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `request_log_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_feedback` (\n  `feedback_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `comment` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rating` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`feedback_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_feedback_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
